{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>Who brought you out, etc.</b> Just as I distinguished between firstborn and non-firstborn, so I know and exact retribution from the one who lends money to Israel at interest and claims it belongs to a gentile. Another interpretation: ״who brought you out of the land of Egypt״ — on condition that you accept My commandments upon yourselves, even if they are burdensome upon you." "<b>To give you the land of Canaan.</b> As reward for your accepting My commandments." "<b>To be to you for an Elohim.</b> Whoever dwells in the land of Israel — I am to him for an Elohim; and whoever leaves it is like one who worships idols. (Sifra; Ketubot 110)"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The first interpretation reads the verse as an allusion to God's precision in distinguishing details; the link to the preceding laws of lending at interest (v. 36–37) is implicit."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:26.176559723Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}